cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this proof using the metadata below and identify the commit consulted."
title: "Real-Rootedness of the Type B Eulerian Transformation on the Cone P_n"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Ozols
    given-names: Chris
    website: "https://github.com/cozuya"
url: "https://github.com/cozuya/eulerian-transformation-type-b"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cozuya/eulerian-transformation-type-b"
abstract: >-
  A Lean-checked proof of the Eulerian-map part of Athanasiadis's Remark 7.2(b)
  (On the real-rootedness of the Eulerian transformation): if B is the linear
  map with B(t^m) = B_m(x), the type B Eulerian polynomial, then for every n
  and every nonzero nonnegative c_0, ..., c_n the polynomial
  B(sum_k c_k t^(n-k) (1+t)^k) has only real roots; it has degree n and all
  roots are negative. Simple roots, interlacing of the basis images, the larger
  cone and the derangement map are given only informally. By Chris Ozols, with
  AI-assisted proof development and formalization; the Lean formalization was
  written by Anthropic's Claude on top of the RealRooted library. Verified with
  Lean 4.35.0, Mathlib v4.35.0 and RealRooted d667074, using only the standard
  axioms propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. The remark reports the
  statement as supported by computational evidence. Possible overlap with Liu
  and Yan (Adv. in Appl. Math. 162, 2025) is unresolved. No claim of novelty,
  first discovery, or historical priority.
keywords:
  - type B Eulerian polynomials
  - Eulerian transformation
  - real-rooted polynomials
  - interlacing
  - signed permutations
  - Athanasiadis Remark 7.2
  - Euler numerator
  - Brändén
  - Lean
  - Mathlib
  - RealRooted
  - formal proof
